  "id": "COMPOUND:16884 - PROTEIN:4915",
  "verbalization": "Dieckol is implicated in the biological pathway leading to Replicase polyprotein 1ab through a series of targets, primarily the H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3. This transporter is targeted by Norarecoline, which in turn targets Replicase polyprotein 1ab. The evidence suggests a potential mechanism where Dieckol may influence the activity of the H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3, thereby modulating the function of Replicase polyprotein 1ab. The indirect relationship is supported by the presence of a second, less well-characterized target of Dieckol, which also leads to Replicase polyprotein 1ab. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Dieckol in regulating the replicase complex, potentially through interactions with ion transporters. The evidence supports a mechanism where Dieckol may act as a modulator of the replicase polyprotein 1ab through a chain of targets involving ion transporters.",
